<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Discussion</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Visual-TableQA vs ReachQA</h3>

<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Performance of fine-tuned models on the two splits of the ReachQA test set: <span id="S4.T4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Recognition</span> (Reco) and <span id="S4.T4.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reasoning</span> (Reas), each consisting of exactly 1,000 samples. Best performances per model category are in <span id="S4.T4.17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>. The values in <span id="S4.T4.17.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">blue</span> are from our own evaluation using the LLM jury, while the remaining values are taken from  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al. ()</a></cite>.</span></figcaption>
